hands is based on the pi-env daemon of Pi (https://github.com/earendil-works/pi, packages/env/daemon) by Mario
Zechner, Armin Ronacher and Earendil Works. Its source files in src/ (all except cli.rs, install.rs, jobs.rs,
main.rs, state.rs, supervisor.rs and ui/) and docs/protocol.md and docs/semantics.md come from pi-env, with these
changes: the crate and binary are named hands, the Windows backend was removed, main.rs became serve.rs, and serve
gained the job.* and ui.* operations (docs/jobs.md). pi-env is used under the following license:

